# An indented `from` line still starts a new query, with a certain `;` (D-037).
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | extend c = a + 1
    from u | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..46
  PIPELINE@0..25
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    EXTEND_OP@9..25
      IDENT@9..15 "extend"
      WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@16..25
        NAME@16..17
          IDENT@16..17 "c"
        WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
        EQ@18..19 "="
        WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
        BIN_EXPR@20..25
          NAME_REF@20..21
            IDENT@20..21 "a"
          WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
          PLUS@22..23 "+"
          WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
          LITERAL@24..25
            LONG@24..25 "1"
  WHITESPACE@25..30 "\n    "
  PIPELINE@30..45
    IDENT@30..34 "from"
    WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
    NAME_REF@35..36
      IDENT@35..36 "u"
    WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
    PIPE@37..38 "|"
    WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
    TAKE_OP@39..45
      IDENT@39..43 "take"
      WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
      LITERAL@44..45
        LONG@44..45 "5"
  WHITESPACE@45..46 "\n"

error[DS0106]: missing `;` between statements
  --> query:1:26
  |
1 | from t | extend c = a + 1
  |                          ^ expected `;` here
2 |     from u | take 5
  |     ---- a new statement starts here
  |
  = help: end the statement with `;`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | extend c = a + 1;
        from u | take 5
which parses without errors
